# ── Huff workspace ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo versions the WORKSPACE-LEVEL assets: the agent charters, the
# routing CLAUDE.md, the Money kit, and Channel Lab. It deliberately does NOT
# swallow the application projects — they are 43G/5.8G/3.4G of databases and
# two of them already have their own git history.

# Projects with their OWN repositories — never absorb their working trees into
# the Huff workspace repository. Gojo's small workspace manifest is tracked;
# its four Git worktrees remain owned by the separate trading-os repository.
/trading-os/
/Gojo/trading_personal/
/Gojo/gojo_stage/
/Gojo/gojo_prod/

# Heavy application projects (databases, renders, node_modules).
# Random Project alone carries a ~15G SQLite file; Faceless carries renders.
/Random Project/
/Faceless/

# Budget app: track the source, never the data or deps.
/Huff House Budget/node_modules/
/Huff House Budget/data/

# Machine-local Claude state — settings.local.json holds per-machine paths and
# permissions, and command/session artefacts are not shared assets.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent memory lives in ONE store: Gojo/trading_personal/.claude/agent-memory (per-seat memory.db + notes, AGENTS.md §9).
# The harness's `memory: project` dir is <session cwd>/.claude/agent-memory, so this path is a SYMLINK to that store
# (2026-10-02, backend-lead lane bl/memory-home-1001; Kyle: "my agent memory folder doesnt line up with how many agents
# I have"). No trailing slash: a `dir/` pattern does not match a symlink (F-445). The renamed-aside empty tree too.
/.claude/agent-memory
/.claude/agent-memory.pre-symlink-*

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.log

# Never version data or secrets, anywhere, at any depth.
**/node_modules/
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/backups/

# Gojo runtime data, never source (2026-10-01; Kyle: "when is the huff repo going to get cleaned up").
# Moved-out prod data (the 09-25 build-surface moves), promote rollback builds, and agent memory notes that
# landed at the Gojo root instead of trading_personal's per-seat stores (T-review-lead-010 owns that drift).
/Gojo/.gojo-prod-data/
/Gojo/.gojo-rollback-store/
/Gojo/.claude/
